<h2 id="ha-ctrl-009-acceptance">Acceptance and evidence</h2>

1. Create an unsaved draft, undo a change, save successfully and reject a save. Verify the actual retained draft and distinguish it from persisted configuration.
2. Navigate nested conditions/actions, move and delete blocks using the native keyboard routes. Preserve focus and execution order; record unresolved limitations.
3. Review an action-only test and a real triggered trace separately. Confirm which branches/targets each evaluates in a controlled environment.
4. Test disabled, enabled, currently running and deleted automation states, plus concurrent edits and connection loss. No save/test action should be dispatched from these documentation examples.

Record the integration/frontend version, browser, fixture or device, input state, expected result, observed result and evidence location. Source review and documentation checks are not live-device verification. Record unresolved native limitations explicitly; do not turn this checklist into an accessibility guarantee.

